! FS_COMP: Compression (upper) envelope of suspension spring force (1 side). Spring
! force can be a nonlinear CARPET function of static spring force and spring
! compression or a function of spring compression (CONSTANT, COEFFICIENT, or TABLE)
! combined with a function FS_COMP_FSTATIC of static spring force (CONSTANT,
! COEFFICIENT, or TABLE). Spring force from the calculation can be adjusted with
! FS_COMP_GAIN and FS_COMP_OFFSET. Spring compression used in the calculation can be
! adjusted with CMP_SCALE_FS_COMP and CMP_START_FS_COMP. Static spring force used in
! the calculation can be adjusted with FSTATIC_SCALE_FS_COMP and
! FSTATIC_START_FS_COMP. An inverse version of this function is used internally. This
! configurable function supports 6 datasets; if indices shown below are not used,
! e.g., (1,1,2), the current values of the indices IUNIT, IAXLE, and ISIDE are used
! to identify the dataset when reading data.

FS_COMP_COEFFICIENT(1,1,1) 198 ! Spring force per unit spring compression (N/mm),
                               ! unit 1, axle 1, left side
FS_COMP_GAIN(1,1,1) 1 ! [D] Multiplied with calculated value to get spring force
FS_COMP_OFFSET(1,1,1) 20 ; N ! Added (after gain) to get spring force
CMP_START_FS_COMP(1,1,1) 0 ; mm ! [D] Subtracted from spring compression
CMP_SCALE_FS_COMP(1,1,1) 1 ! [D] Divided into (spring compression -
                           ! CMP_START_FS_COMP)
FS_COMP_COMBINE(1,1,1) MULTIPLY ! [D] How to combine the two components
FS_COMP_FSTATIC_CONSTANT(1,1,1) 1 ; - ! [D] Spring force component due to static
                                  ! spring force, unit 1, axle 1, left side

FS_COMP_COEFFICIENT(1,1,2) 198 ! Spring force per unit spring compression (N/mm),
                               ! unit 1, axle 1, right side
FS_COMP_GAIN(1,1,2) 1 ! [D] Multiplied with calculated value to get spring force
FS_COMP_OFFSET(1,1,2) 20 ; N ! Added (after gain) to get spring force
CMP_START_FS_COMP(1,1,2) 0 ; mm ! [D] Subtracted from spring compression
CMP_SCALE_FS_COMP(1,1,2) 1 ! [D] Divided into (spring compression -
                           ! CMP_START_FS_COMP)
FS_COMP_COMBINE(1,1,2) MULTIPLY ! [D] How to combine the two components
FS_COMP_FSTATIC_CONSTANT(1,1,2) 1 ; - ! [D] Spring force component due to static
                                  ! spring force, unit 1, axle 1, right side

